---
import WorkingGroupInterestForm from '@/components/campaign/WorkingGroupInterestForm.astro';
import BrandHeading from '@/components/BrandHeading.astro';
import { contributionOptions, workingGroupContexts } from '@/data/working-group-campaign';
import StandalonePublicLayout from '@/layouts/StandalonePublicLayout.astro';
import '@/styles/working-group-join.css';
import '@/styles/working-group-campaign.css';
import '@/styles/working-group-campaign-sections.css';
import '@/styles/working-group-campaign-responsive.css';

const privacyNoticeVersion = '2026-08-13';
const title = 'Join an SPDTF working group';
const description = 'Bring your professional experience to the industry working groups helping to develop the Smart Property Data Trust Framework.';
---
<StandalonePublicLayout
  title={title}
  description={description}
  bodyClass="working-group-campaign"
  socialImage="/images/working-group-recruitment-social.png"
>
  <div class="wg-page">
    <section class="wg-campaign-hero" aria-labelledby="join-title">
      <div class="wg-campaign-hero__copy">
        <a class="wg-hero-brand-link" href="/" aria-label="Open Property Data Association home">
          <BrandHeading surface="dark" campaign />
        </a>
        <p class="wg-eyebrow wg-eyebrow--hero">The property industry, working together</p>
        <h1 id="join-title">Help shape the future of <em>property information sharing.</em></h1>
        <p class="wg-lead">
          The way property information is prepared, checked and shared is changing. Bring the
          commercial reality, professional judgement or public-interest perspective that future
          requirements need to work in practice.
        </p>
        <div class="wg-hero-actions">
          <a class="btn wg-btn--large" href="#register">Register your interest <span aria-hidden="true">↓</span></a>
        </div>
        <p class="wg-hero-note">
          No data expertise is required. What matters is your first-hand understanding of how the property industry works.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="wg-hero-journey" aria-labelledby="influence-title">
        <p class="wg-eyebrow">What you can contribute</p>
        <h2 id="influence-title">Help make the framework work in practice.</h2>
        <ol class="wg-process">
          <li><strong>Share how your sector works</strong><span>Describe the language, rules, incentives and exceptions that shape day-to-day decisions.</span></li>
          <li><strong>Challenge costly assumptions</strong><span>Identify gaps, unintended consequences and requirements that would be difficult to implement.</span></li>
          <li><strong>Test proposals in practice</strong><span>Check whether proposed guidance and data outputs would improve familiar services and processes.</span></li>
        </ol>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section id="why-this-matters" class="wg-section wg-motivation" aria-labelledby="motivation-title">
      <div class="wg-section__heading">
        <div>
          <p class="wg-eyebrow">Why take part</p>
          <h2 id="motivation-title">This is about making change work for the people who have to make it work.</h2>
        </div>
        <div>
          <p>
            Better property information is not just a technical question. It affects cost, risk,
            customer experience, professional responsibility and the services businesses can offer.
            The working groups are where those realities can shape the work.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="wg-motivation-grid">
        <article>
          <span>Commercial operators</span>
          <h3>Protect the operating reality</h3>
          <p>Bring the costs, incentives, supplier dependencies and implementation pressures that a proposal must understand to be viable.</p>
        </article>
        <article>
          <span>Professionals</span>
          <h3>Make practice workable</h3>
          <p>Help ensure definitions, evidence and processes reflect real cases—not only the straightforward ones on paper.</p>
        </article>
        <article>
          <span>Technology and data teams</span>
          <h3>Build for the systems people use</h3>
          <p>Test whether new information can be exchanged reliably, proportionately and affordably across existing services.</p>
        </article>
        <article>
          <span>Public-interest voices</span>
          <h3>Design in trust and inclusion</h3>
          <p>Make consumer outcomes, accessibility, safeguards and non-digital needs visible from the beginning.</p>
        </article>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="wg-policy" aria-labelledby="policy-title">
      <div class="wg-policy__inner">
        <div>
          <p class="wg-eyebrow">Why now</p>
          <h2 id="policy-title">The direction of travel is clear. The practical detail is still open.</h2>
        </div>
        <div class="wg-policy__copy">
          <p>
            Government is pursuing home-buying reform and wider Smart Data policy. The Data (Use and
            Access) Act 2025 provides the framework for Smart Data schemes, while property-specific
            arrangements remain prospective and subject to evidence, consultation and further decisions.
          </p>
          <p>
            That is why practitioner input matters now: it can help future requirements work for the
            organisations and people affected by them, rather than asking them to adapt to untested assumptions.
          </p>
          <a href="/programme">Understand the programme and policy context <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a>
        </div>
        <ol class="wg-policy__markers" aria-label="Programme and policy context">
          <li><span>Direction</span><strong>Home-buying reform and Smart Data policy are moving forward.</strong></li>
          <li><span>Opportunity</span><strong>Property-specific rules and standards are still being explored.</strong></li>
          <li><span>Role</span><strong>Working groups test what will be useful, proportionate and trusted.</strong></li>
        </ol>
        <p class="wg-policy__status">SPDTF is an industry programme in development. It is not a government-approved or adopted statutory scheme.</p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section id="groups" class="wg-section wg-groups" aria-labelledby="groups-title">
      <div class="wg-section__heading">
        <div>
          <p class="wg-eyebrow">Find your place</p>
          <h2 id="groups-title">Choose the part of the property journey you know best.</h2>
        </div>
        <div>
          <p>
            The groups bring together people who understand distinct parts of the property journey.
            Join one or more where your experience can make the difference between a plausible idea
            and a practical outcome.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="wg-group-grid">
        {workingGroupContexts.map((context) => (
          <article class="wg-group-card">
            <h3>{context.label}</h3>
            <p>{context.scope}</p>
            <a href="#register" data-context-register={context.value}>I’m interested in {context.label}</a>
          </article>
        ))}
      </div>
      <aside class="wg-cross-cutting" aria-labelledby="cross-cutting-title">
        <p class="wg-eyebrow">Experience that crosses every group</p>
        <h3 id="cross-cutting-title">Commercial and public interests both belong in the room.</h3>
        <p>You do not need to fit neatly into one professional group. Your business experience, consumer perspective, accessibility expertise or regulatory insight can help make the work stronger.</p>
      </aside>
    </section>

    <section class="wg-participation" aria-labelledby="participation-title">
      <div class="wg-participation__intro">
        <div>
          <p class="wg-eyebrow">What you can influence</p>
          <h2 id="participation-title">Bring experience. Improve the proposal. Change what will matter.</h2>
        </div>
        <p>
          The work is presented in language that practitioners can review. Technical teams turn agreed
          meaning into standards and tools; your role is to make sure the meaning and result are right
          for your field, your organisation and the people it serves.
        </p>
      </div>

      <ol class="wg-participation-steps">
          <li><span>01</span><strong>Define what matters</strong><p>Make the language, evidence and outcomes that matter in your field clear.</p></li>
          <li><span>02</span><strong>Review the proposal</strong><p>Check draft definitions, examples and questions against everyday practice.</p></li>
          <li><span>03</span><strong>Challenge weak assumptions</strong><p>Identify missing rules, hidden costs, edge cases and unintended consequences.</p></li>
          <li><span>04</span><strong>Test a practical result</strong><p>Tell us whether future guidance, data outputs and services make sense in real work.</p></li>
      </ol>

      <div class="wg-participation-grid">
        <div>
          <p class="wg-eyebrow">Ways to contribute</p>
          <h3>Your contribution can match your experience and availability.</h3>
        </div>
        <ul>
          {contributionOptions.map((option) => (
            <li><strong>{option.label}</strong><span>{option.description}</span></li>
          ))}
        </ul>
      </div>

      <div class="wg-commitment">
        <strong>Before you commit</strong>
        <p>
          If your expression of interest is accepted, OPDA will confirm the group format, schedule
          and expectations before asking you to commit. Registering now does not commit you to take part.
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="wg-section wg-evidence" aria-labelledby="trust-title">
      <div class="wg-evidence__statement">
          <p class="wg-eyebrow">A contribution with boundaries</p>
          <h2 id="trust-title">Your judgement is valuable. Your authority is respected.</h2>
        <p>
          Existing documents show what has been recorded. Practitioners understand why it matters,
          where exceptions arise and what happens when a rule does not fit real work.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="wg-evidence__reasons">
        <article><span>Practice</span><h3>Explain the real meaning</h3><p>Make language, rules and exceptions visible beyond your field.</p></article>
        <article><span>Commercial reality</span><h3>Surface the trade-offs</h3><p>Make sure cost, operational impact and incentives are part of the conversation.</p></article>
        <article><span>Public interest</span><h3>Protect people and outcomes</h3><p>Bring consumer, accessibility, regulatory and public-interest needs into the work.</p></article>
        <article><span>Practical value</span><h3>Test what will be useful</h3><p>Check whether the intended result can support familiar work and services.</p></article>
      </div>

      <div class="wg-trust">
        <div>
          <p class="wg-eyebrow">Clear boundaries</p>
          <h3>Interest is reviewed by people.</h3>
          <p>
            Share only what you and your organisation are authorised to share. Source material is
            reviewed and is not automatically published.
          </p>
        </div>
        <ul>
          <li>SPDTF is in development; participation does not make it adopted or confer standards authority.</li>
          <li>No data-modelling or technical knowledge is required.</li>
          <li>AI may assist comparison and drafting; it cannot make a draft official.</li>
          <li>Registration is an expression of interest, not membership, access, a vote or permission to represent your employer.</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </section>

    <WorkingGroupInterestForm
      contexts={workingGroupContexts}
      contributions={contributionOptions}
      privacyNoticeVersion={privacyNoticeVersion}
    />
  </div>
  <script>
    import '@/scripts/working-group-join';
    import '@/scripts/working-group-campaign';
  </script>
  <script is:inline src="/ui/client.js"></script>
</StandalonePublicLayout>

<style>
  :global(.working-group-campaign .campaign-masthead) {
    position: absolute;
    inset: 0 0 auto;
    justify-content: flex-end;
    background: transparent;
    border-bottom: 0;
  }

  :global(.working-group-campaign .campaign-masthead__brand) { display: none; }
  :global(.working-group-campaign .campaign-masthead__nav) { margin-left: auto; }

  :global(.working-group-campaign .wg-campaign-hero) {
    min-height: min(48rem, 100svh);
    padding-top: var(--space-6);
  }

  .wg-hero-brand-link {
    display: inline-block;
    color: inherit;
    text-decoration: none;
  }

  .wg-hero-brand-link:hover {
    color: inherit;
    text-decoration: none;
  }

  .wg-eyebrow--hero {
    font-size: clamp(var(--text-sm), 1.1vw, var(--text-base));
  }
</style>
